---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import PolicyArticle from '../components/PolicyArticle.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
import { policyLastUpdated, sitePayments, siteTracking } from '../data/policies';
import { hasContactFormEndpoint, hasPublicCalUrl } from '../data/integrations';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | She Who Remembers"
  description="How this website handles information you choose to share, what is not collected here, and how booking or contact tools work when they are connected."
>
  <Hero
    heading="Privacy"
    lede="What this site may collect, and what it is not built to collect."
    surface="light"
    spacing="compact"
  >
    <p>
      This page describes the website as it actually works. It is a visitor-facing policy, not
      legal advice, and it is not presented as a lawyer-reviewed document.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <PolicyArticle lastUpdated={policyLastUpdated}>
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          She Who Remembers is a static website. It does not currently run a client database, a
          payment checkout, or its own analytics. Information reaches this project only when you
          choose to send it through a connected contact form, or when you leave the site to use
          an external booking calendar.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a tool is not connected yet, this page will not pretend that collection is happening.
        </p>

        <h2>Information you choose to provide</h2>
        <p>
          You are not required to create an account to read this site. The information this
          project may receive is limited to what you voluntarily submit through a connected
          contact form, and what you share with an external booking provider if you schedule a
          conversation.
        </p>

        <h2>Booking information</h2>
        {
          hasPublicCalUrl ? (
            <p>
              Scheduling currently happens through an external booking provider. When you open
              that calendar, you leave this website. The provider may collect information such as
              your name, email, and appointment details according to its own practices. She Who
              Remembers does not store that provider&apos;s booking records on this website.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              No live booking calendar is connected on this site yet. When scheduling is
              connected, it will happen through an external booking provider. This website is not
              built to store that provider&apos;s appointment records.
            </p>
          )
        }
        <p>
          Any confirmation email about a booked time would come from the calendar you used, not
          from this website.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact-form information</h2>
        {
          hasContactFormEndpoint ? (
            <>
              <p>When you send a message through the contact form, the fields are:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Name</li>
                <li>Email</li>
                <li>Reason for writing</li>
                <li>Message</li>
              </ul>
              <p>
                Those fields are posted to an external static-form provider so the message can be
                delivered. This website does not keep its own inbox or message archive.
              </p>
            </>
          ) : (
            <p>
              Message submission is not active on this site yet. When the contact form is
              connected, it may collect name, email, reason for writing, and message, and post
              those fields to an external static-form provider. This website is not built to keep
              its own inbox.
            </p>
          )
        }

        <h2>Technical information</h2>
        <p>
          Ordinary web delivery can include technical details such as IP address, browser type,
          requested page, and approximate time of the request. Those details may be processed by
          the hosting environment as part of serving static files. This project does not currently
          run its own analytics on that information.
        </p>
        {
          siteTracking.firstPartyAnalytics ? (
            <p>First-party analytics are enabled on this site.</p>
          ) : (
            <p>No first-party analytics tool is integrated on this website at this time.</p>
          )
        }

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>This site currently loads webfonts from Google Fonts. That service may receive technical information such as IP address when a page is viewed.</p>
        <p>
          Depending on what is connected, visitors may also encounter:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>an external booking provider, when scheduling is active</li>
          <li>an external static-form provider, when contact delivery is active</li>
          <li>a future payment processor, if paid offerings are later configured</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Those services have their own practices. This page does not control them and does not
          name a live provider until one is actually configured.
        </p>
        {
          siteTracking.firstPartyTrackingCookies ? (
            <p>This site sets first-party tracking cookies.</p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              This website does not currently set first-party tracking cookies. Third-party
              services you visit (including a booking calendar, a form provider, or Google Fonts)
              may use their own cookies or similar technologies.
            </p>
          )
        }

        <h2>Data minimization</h2>
        <p>
          Ask only for what a reply or a booking actually needs. Do not send records this site is
          not built to hold. The contact form is for practical messages, not for coaching intake
          files or confidential case material.
        </p>

        <h2>Sensitive information</h2>
        <p>Please do not submit confidential material through the general contact form, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>medical records</li>
          <li>psychiatric records</li>
          <li>diagnosis details</li>
          <li>legal case materials</li>
          <li>crisis disclosures</li>
          <li>payment card information</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The form is not monitored as emergency support. If you are in immediate danger, contact
          local emergency services or a trusted local resource.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
          This website does not currently keep its own archive of contact messages or booking
          records. If a form or booking provider is connected, that provider&apos;s retention
          practices apply. Specific retention periods are not listed here because they depend on
          a provider that has not been named on this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          A static site has a smaller surface than an application that stores accounts or card
          data. That is not a promise that information can never be misused, intercepted, or
          mishandled by a third party you choose to use. Do not send payment card numbers or
          confidential records through this website.
        </p>
        {
          sitePayments.publicCheckoutActive ? (
            <p>A public payment checkout is active. Card data would be handled by the payment processor, not stored as ordinary website content.</p>
          ) : (
            <p>No public payment checkout is currently active on this site, and this website is not built to store payment card data.</p>
          )
        }

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>
          Links to other sites, including a future booking calendar or purchase page, lead to
          places this project does not operate. Their privacy practices are their own.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This website is intended for adults. It is not directed at children, and it is not
          designed to collect information from children.
        </p>

        <h2>Policy updates</h2>
        <p>
          This page may change as the site changes. The date at the top of the article is the
          last time this wording was intentionally updated. It does not change automatically
          with every build.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact about privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy can be sent through the{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact</TextLink> page. There is no separate
          public privacy email published on this site.
        </p>
      </PolicyArticle>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If you need the practical door"
    primary={{ label: 'Contact', href: withBase('/contact') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Coaching Disclaimer', href: withBase('/coaching-disclaimer') }}
  >
    <p>Scope lives beside privacy. Both are part of using this work honestly.</p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>
